3ba91_onyx_blog-thumbnail_tales-from-the-runtime-layer-p-800.webp 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/69a56ea6fdb0bd37931fda86/6a503169a13f3c511e53ba91_onyx_blog-thumbnail_tales-from-the-runtime-layer.webp 1196w\"></div><div class=\"blog-item-card-text-c\"><div class=\"blog-item-card-auth-c\"><div>20 May 2026</div><div>⸱</div><div>Stephen Fitzgerald</div></div><h3 class=\"blog-card-title\">Tales from the Runtime Layer: Why Authorized Agents Break Your Security and Your Infrastructure</h3><p>Authorized agents can exfiltrate data and break infrastructure while using legitimate permissions – and your existing security stack won't see it coming.</p></div></a>","link":"https://www.onyx.security/blog/tales-from-the-runtime-layer-why-authorized-agents-break-your-security-and-your-infrastructure","retrieved":1779235200000},{"title":"Four Guardrails: The Customer Success Pattern for Safe AI Agent Adoption","contents":"<a href=\"/blog/four-guardrails-the-customer-success-pattern-for-safe-ai-agent-adoption\" class=\"blog-item-card w-inline-block\"><div class=\"blog-item-card-img-c\"><img src=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/69a56ea6fdb0bd37931fda86/6a458299b1ad2311ad8516fc_Four%20Guardrails_%20The%20Customer%20Success%20Pattern%20for%20Safe%20AI%20Agent%20Adoption.avif\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Knitted-yarn illustration of an archway strung with four horizontal rails, each holding a colored padlock, set against a soft blue sky with woolly clouds.\"></div><div class=\"blog-item-card-text-c\"><div class=\"blog-item-card-auth-c\"><div>06 May 2026</div><div>⸱</div><div>Christopher DiClerico</div></div><h3 class=\"blog-card-title\">Four Guardrails: The Customer Success Pattern for Safe AI Agent Adoption</h3><p>Discovery, runtime enforcement, session logging, and MCP server control – the four operational guardrails every customer deploys in week one to govern agents already running.</p></div></a>","link":"https://www.onyx.security/blog/four-guardrails-the-customer-success-pa